SUMMARY:🍂🌿 NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park 🌿🍂
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂🌿 **NEW FALL WALK: Discov
 er Biidaasige Park** 🌿🍂\n\n### A Brand-New Toronto Park\, Fall Colou
 rs & Waterfront Trails\n\nWe're trying something **new**!\n\nJoin us for o
 ur first group walk to **Biidaasige Park**\, one of the newest and most am
 bitious parks in Toronto. Opened as part of the massive transformation of 
 the Port Lands\, the park sits on **Ookwemin Minising**\, Toronto's new is
 land where the Don River meets Lake Ontario.\n\nThis isn't a walk we've do
 ne before\, which makes it a little more exciting. We'll spend much of the
  afternoon actually **exploring the park rather than rushing through it** 
 — following its trails\, enjoying the waterfront\, taking in the fall sc
 enery\, and stopping along the way to appreciate the new landscape.\nThe p
 ark is enormous\, with more than **50 acres already open** and more sectio
 ns being added as the Port Lands transformation continues.\n\nThere are cu
 rated trails and paths\, viewpoints\, natural areas\, and places to get do
 wn closer to the new Don River.\nAnd because we're doing this in the fall\
 , we'll get to experience the park at a completely different time of year 
 — cooler air\, changing leaves\, open skies\, and fewer summer crowds. 
 🍂\n\nWe'll meet at the **Young Centre in the Distillery District** simp
 ly because it's an easy and convenient meeting point before we head toward
  the park. We won't be spending the day touring the Distillery District 
 — **the park is the destination.**\n\n📲 **Don't Forget to join our Wh
 atsApp Group – [\\[CLICK HERE!\\]](http://xn--%5Bclick%20here!%5D(%20joi
 n%20our%20whatsapp%20group-cu832c:%20Click%20here%20to%20join)/)**\n\n***\
 n\n## 🚶‍♂️ **What We'll Do**\n\nWe'll meet outside the **Young Ce
 ntre for the Performing Arts** and make our way toward Biidaasige Park.\nO
 nce we reach the park\, we'll slow things down and spend about **90 minute
 s exploring the trails and waterfront**.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* 🍂 E
 njoy the fall colours\n* 🌿 Explore the park's trails and green spaces\n
 * 🌊 Walk along the new waterfront landscape\n* 📸 Stop for photos and
  scenic views\n* 🌳 Explore the natural areas around the new Don River\n
 * 🌆 Take in views toward the Toronto skyline and Toronto Islands\n* 
 🚶‍♂️ Enjoy plenty of time to walk and talk with the group\n\nThe 
 walk itself will be approximately **2 hours**\, but we're not trying to ra
 ce through it.\n**This is about experiencing the park.**\nIt's our first t
 ime doing this walk\, so we'll take our time and actually enjoy discoverin
 g what has been created here.\n\n***\n\n## 🌊 **Why Biidaasige Park?**\n
 \nBiidaasige Park is part of one of the biggest transformations Toronto ha
 s seen in decades.\nThe new Don River was created as part of the Port Land
 s Flood Protection project\, transforming former industrial land into a ne
 w river valley\, wetlands\, parkland and public spaces.\n\nThe first phase
  of Biidaasige Park opened in July 2025.\nThe park includes **accessible t
 rails\, cycling paths\, river access\, wetlands\, viewpoints and waterfron
 t promenades**\, with views toward the Toronto Islands\, Inner Harbour and
  skyline.\n\nAnd there's something particularly fun about visiting a place
  that is still **brand new**.\nWe're not revisiting an old Toronto favouri
 te.\n**We're discovering somewhere new together.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 **Aft
 er the Walk: The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**\n\nAfter exploring the park
 \, we'll head over to **The Keating Channel Pub & Grill** for lunch.\nThe 
 pub sits right on the Keating Channel and has been a local fixture in the 
 area for more than 20 years. After years of Port Lands construction made t
 he neighbourhood difficult to reach\, the transformation of the area has b
 rought new life and new visitors back to the waterfront.\nIt's a nice way 
 to finish the day: **a brand-new park followed by one of the neighbourhood
 's old survivors.**\nLunch is optional\, but everyone is welcome to join u
 s.\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 **Fall Weather & Expectations**\n\nThis is a **social
  urban walk**\, not a difficult hike.\nWe'll be walking for approximately 
 two hours\, including our time exploring the park\, so you should be comfo
 rtable being on your feet for that length of time.\nPlease dress for typic
 al Toronto fall weather. The waterfront can be cooler and windier than oth
 er parts of the city\, so a warm layer is a good idea.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 *
 *Meetup Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside the **Young Centre 
 for the Performing Arts**\, 50 Tank House Lane\, in the Distillery Distric
 t. Young Centre for the Performing Arts\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Ha
 t!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.
 \n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** The Keating 
 Channel Pub & Grill\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ **Meetup Fee**\n\n**$5 cash in pe
 rson or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps s
 upport the group and allows us to continue organizing walks and events thr
 oughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 **What to Bring**\n\n💧 Water\n👟 C
 omfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\
 n📸 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 **Who Is This For?
 **\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy discovering new places
  in Toronto\n* Anyone who likes parks and waterfront trails\n* People who 
 want a relaxed social walk\n* Anyone interested in seeing Toronto's newest
  public spaces\n* People who enjoy exploring somewhere they've never been 
 before\n* Anyone who wants to spend a fall day outside with good people\n\
 nThe park may be new.\n**The idea is the same: come out\, walk with us\, a
 nd meet some people along the way.**\n\n***\n\n📲 **You're welcome to RS
 VP ahead of time — or just show up on the day if you're unsure about you
 r schedule.**\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled
  or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤
  **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n
 📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come discover a new park
 .**\n**Stay for the fall colours.**\n**Stay a little longer for lunch and 
 friendship.** 🍂🌿🍺
