SUMMARY:👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto🌙!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto 
 🌙\n\n### Haunted Hotels\, Dark History & The Ghosts of Downtown\n\nToro
 nto has a long history — and some of it is considerably darker than the 
 history books make it sound.\n\nJoin us for an evening walk through **Old 
 Toronto**\, where we'll uncover stories of haunted hotels\, gruesome execu
 tions\, mysterious deaths\, and some of the stranger legends that have bec
 ome part of the city's history.\nWe'll walk through the downtown core as t
 he city settles into the evening\, stopping along the way for stories abou
 t the ghosts\, tragedies\, and unusual events connected to the streets and
  buildings around us.\nAnd yes\, we'll even explore **why Toronto has a lo
 ng-standing fear of clowns.** 🤡👻\n\nThis isn't simply a walk through
  downtown.\nIt's a **curated storytelling experience** that looks at some 
 of Toronto's history from a decidedly darker perspective.\n\n📱 Don't fo
 rget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.c
 om/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll
  begin outside the **Royal York Hotel** and make our way through Old Toron
 to toward the **Hockey Hall of Fame**.\nAlong the way\, we'll hear stories
  about:\n\n* 🤡 **Why Toronto doesn't like clowns**\n* 🏨 **The ghosts
  of downtown's historic hotels**\n* 💀 **Gruesome executions and forgott
 en tragedies**\n* 🔫 **A deadly reminder of why you should never play wi
 th guns**\n* 👻 **Restless spirits and strange encounters**\n* 🕯️ A
 nd much\, much more…\n\nWe'll remain outside throughout the experience a
 nd **will not be entering the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ A Little A
 bout the Experience\n\nThis is one of our **curated ghost walks**\, rather
  than a regular social walk.\nI've researched the stories\, developed the 
 route\, and brought together some of the stranger pieces of Toronto's hist
 ory to create an evening experience that is part history\, part ghost stor
 y\, and part “what the hell happened here?”\nYou don't have to believe
  in ghosts.\n**You just have to enjoy a good story.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 
 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the **Royal Y
 ork Hotel**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** *
 *6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On 
 time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End P
 oint:** **Hockey Hall of Fame**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 c
 ash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is
  a **curated ghost-walking experience**\, rather than one of our regular s
 ocial walks. The route\, stories\, and history have been researched and br
 ought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support th
 e time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 Wha
 t to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clo
 thing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is Thi
 s For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost st
 ories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's history\n* 🕯️ Fans of
  the strange and unexplained\n* 🤡 People brave enough to learn about To
 ronto's clown problem\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for something different to do
  in the evening\n* 😂 People who enjoy being a little creeped out withou
 t taking it too seriously\n\n***\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for 
 the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.
 ** 👻🌙\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time o
 r just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes
  things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please 
 keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n
 Questions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandouting
 s@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories
 .**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙
