SUMMARY:Social Fluency: Halloween Edition 🎃
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHalloween weekend is the MOST soci
 al event of the year and it’s a time when strangers expect to talk to ea
 ch other. Let's make sure you're ready.\n\nWhat do you have planned? A cos
 tume party\, a bar crawl\, a work event\, or maybe you’re handing out ca
 ndy to the neighbors\, whatever you are getting up to\, the whole weekend 
 is packed with chances to meet people. Our 60-minute live\, virtual worksh
 op gets you warmed up before you walk in the door.\n\n**What you’ll walk
  away with**\n\n**The infinite opener in your pocket.** Costumes\, décor\
 , snacks\, and the host are all built-in conversation starters. You'll lea
 rn how to use them\, even if you're not in costume yourself.\n\n**A way to
  keep the conversation going**. No more "nice costume!" followed by an awk
 ward silence. You'll practice turning small talk into a real conversation 
 (and having fun doing it).\n\n**What to do to make sure you see them again
 .** The best party conversations usually die on November 1st. You'll learn
  how to turn a good chat into an actual plan\, like a horror movie night\,
  a haunted house\, or a post-Halloween brunch.\n\n**What we’ll do**\n\n*
  Workshop openers live\, with real-time feedback on yours\n* Practice in s
 mall breakout groups\n* Learn how to join a group\, exit gracefully\, and 
 work a room without feeling awkward\n* Pick a weekend mission and go try i
 t out\n\n**This is for you if…**\n\n* You love Halloween but get nervous
  about the social part\n* You tend to end up in the corner of the snack ta
 ble\n* You want to turn "we should hang out sometime" into something that 
 actually happens\n* You're new in town\, rebuilding your social circle\, o
 r just ready to meet more people\n\n**Stop sitting on the sidelines of lif
 e\, jump in and join us!**
